    <div id="root"><div class="min-h-screen flex flex-col bg-bg"><header><nav class="px-gutter py-[18px] flex items-center justify-between"><div class="flex items-center gap-7"><a class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-display text-[21px] font-semibold text-text no-underline leading-none" href="/" data-discover="true" style="letter-spacing: -0.02em;"><span class="w-[3px] h-[18px] bg-vermillion inline-block"></span><span class="translate-y-[1.5px] inline-block">Marketlens</span></a><div class="hidden md:flex items-center gap-7 text-[14px] font-medium text-text-secondary leading-none"><a class="transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-text" href="/data" data-discover="true">Data</a><a class="transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-text" href="/docs" data-discover="true">Documentation</a><a class="transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-text" href="/guides" data-discover="true">Guides</a><a href="/#pricing" class="transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-text">Pricing</a><a class="transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-text" href="/compare" data-discover="true">Compare</a><a href="https://github.com/marketlenstrade/marketlens-python" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-text">GitHub</a></div></div><div class="flex items-center gap-4"><div class="hidden md:block"><a class="text-[13px] font-semibold bg-text text-bg px-5 py-2 transition-opacity duration-200 hover:opacity-85" href="/?signin=1" data-discover="true">Sign in</a></div><button class="md:hidden w-8 h-8 flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-[5px]" aria-label="Open menu"><span class="block w-[18px] h-[2px] bg-text origin-center" style="transform: none;"></span><span class="block w-[18px] h-[2px] bg-text origin-center" style="transform: none;"></span></button></div></nav><div class="border-b border-border"></div></header><main class="flex-1"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What data does Marketlens provide?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Marketlens provides tick-level Polymarket order book snapshots and deltas, executed trades, OHLCV candles, reference prices, and derived signals such as implied probability surfaces across multi-outcome markets. Data is accessed through a Python SDK or a REST API at api.marketlens.trade."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How is this different from Polymarket's own CLOB API?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Polymarket's CLOB API serves current state and trade streams. Marketlens stores full historical order book snapshots and deltas, lets you replay books at millisecond resolution, and exposes derived analytics and a backtesting harness, none of which the upstream CLOB API provides. See marketlens.trade/compare for a comparison with other Polymarket data providers."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I backtest strategies with realistic fills?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The Marketlens backtest harness replays historical order books with real queue priority, configurable latency, and slippage modeling, so fills reflect what your orders would have actually gotten rather than mid-price assumptions."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does Marketlens cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Free tier includes 600 requests/minute and 25M data rows/day with one API key, no card required. Pro is $348/year or $39/month for 3,600 requests/min and 5B rows/month across 5 keys. Scale is $1,788/year or $199/month for 10,800 requests/min and 50B rows/month across 25 keys. All tiers access the same endpoints."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I get started?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Install the Python SDK with `pip install marketlens`, grab a free API key from the console, and you can list markets, fetch order books, and run a backtest in under a minute. See the Getting Started docs at marketlens.trade/docs."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where can I get Polymarket historical order book data?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Marketlens publishes Polymarket order book historical data as tick-level L2 snapshots and deltas at millisecond resolution. Access it via the Python SDK, REST API at api.marketlens.trade/v1, or bulk Parquet exports at marketlens.trade/docs/exports."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Marketlens provide a Polymarket orderbook API?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The Marketlens orderbook API returns full-depth L2 snapshots, lets you walk historical books tick-by-tick, and computes spread, midpoint, and depth metrics. See marketlens.trade/docs/orderbook."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I replay Polymarket order books historically?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The orderbook.walk() endpoint replays Polymarket order books tick-by-tick over any time range, reconstructing book state from stored snapshots and deltas. It powers the backtesting harness and can be used directly for research."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where can I download Polymarket trades history and price data?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Polymarket executed trades and OHLCV candles are available via the /trades and /candles endpoints, or as bulk Parquet exports. Reference prices and midpoints are available at marketlens.trade/docs/reference-prices."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How far back does the Polymarket historical data go?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Order book history starts on 2026-03-01, with continuous coverage since 2026-04-13. The earliest candles date to 2026-02-28, and there are a few gap days in March and April 2026. Esports and standalone event coverage (including the 2028 election markets) begins 2026-08-15. Each market's temporalCoverage field reports its earliest captured snapshot."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a Python SDK for Polymarket market data?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. `pip install marketlens`. The SDK wraps markets, orderbook, trades, candles, exports, reference prices, and a backtesting harness. Source: github.com/marketlenstrade/marketlens-python."}}]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Marketlens","item":"https://marketlens.trade/"}]}</script><section class="py-section px-gutter relative overflow-visible"><canvas class="absolute inset-x-0 top-0 w-full pointer-events-none hidden md:block" aria-hidden="true" width="800" height="624" style="height: 150%;"></canvas><div class="max-w-page mx-auto relative"><div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-gutter"><div><h1 class="font-display text-[32px] md:text-[40px] lg:text-hero text-text" style="opacity: 0; transform: translateY(16px);">Backtest your Polymarket bot on historical order books.</h1><p class="font-body text-[16px] md:text-[18px] text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mt-4" style="opacity: 0; transform: translateY(16px);">Tick-level order book history, backtesting SDK, and structured analytics for Polymarket. From intraday crypto to structured products and live sports.</p><div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start gap-3 mt-6" style="opacity: 0; transform: translateY(16px);"><a class="text-[13px] font-semibold bg-text text-bg px-5 py-2 transition-opacity duration-200 hover:opacity-85 no-underline" href="/?signin=1" data-discover="true">Get API Key</a><a href="/docs" class="text-[13px] font-semibold text-text-secondary border border-border px-5 py-2 transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-text hover:border-text no-underline">Read the Docs</a></div></div><div class="hidden lg:block"></div></div></div></section><section class="py-section px-gutter"><div class="max-w-page mx-auto"><div class="" style="opacity: 0; transform: translateY(16px);"><p class="section-label mb-3">Capabilities</p><h2 class="font-display text-section text-text">Ready to start trading?</h2></div><div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-4 divide-y lg:divide-y-0 lg:divide-x divide-border-light border-y border-border-light"><div class="py-5 lg:px-6 first:lg:pl-0 last:lg:pr-0 transition-colors duration-200 hover:bg-vermillion-soft" style="opacity: 0; transform: translateY(20px);"><p class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-vermillion">Millisecond replay</p><p class="font-body text-[14px] text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mt-2">Replay the full order book at millisecond resolution. Every level, every tick, nothing interpolated.</p></div><div class="py-5 lg:px-6 first:lg:pl-0 last:lg:pr-0 transition-colors duration-200 hover:bg-vermillion-soft" style="opacity: 0; transform: translateY(20px);"><p class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-vermillion">Real-depth backtesting</p><p class="font-body text-[14px] text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mt-2">Backtest against historical books with real queue priority, latency, and slippage.</p></div><div class="py-5 lg:px-6 first:lg:pl-0 last:lg:pr-0 transition-colors duration-200 hover:bg-vermillion-soft" style="opacity: 0; transform: translateY(20px);"><p class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-vermillion">Probability surfaces</p><p class="font-body text-[14px] text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mt-2">Extract implied distributions and survival curves across multi-outcome markets.</p></div><div class="py-5 lg:px-6 first:lg:pl-0 last:lg:pr-0 transition-colors duration-200 hover:bg-vermillion-soft" style="opacity: 0; transform: translateY(20px);"><p class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-vermillion">Self-healing collection</p><p class="font-body text-[14px] text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mt-2">Verified against CLOB ground truth with automatic reseed on drift and redundant connections.</p></div></div></div></section><section aria-label="Platform statistics" class="px-gutter"><div class="max-w-page mx-au